WEBVTT

00:02.410 --> 00:05.380
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.480 --> 00:08.840
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.100 --> 00:10.640
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.480 --> 00:13.250
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.350 --> 00:17.080
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.190 --> 00:20.020
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.390 --> 00:22.020
They are also known as...

00:22.260 --> 00:24.700
the Shinigami.

00:24.960 --> 00:31.630
nureta hitomi no oku

00:24.960 --> 00:31.630
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.340 --> 00:43.650
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.340 --> 00:43.650
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.420 --> 00:42.670
Yami no Matsuei

00:49.960 --> 00:55.830
azayaka na sekai wa

00:49.960 --> 00:55.830
The splendid world

00:58.200 --> 01:08.270
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.200 --> 01:08.270
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.370 --> 01:16.010
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.370 --> 01:16.010
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.110 --> 01:22.640
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.110 --> 01:22.640
A new era beckons now

01:25.360 --> 01:30.450
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.360 --> 01:30.450
The injured black wings

01:30.630 --> 01:37.000
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.630 --> 01:37.000
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.600 --> 01:41.800
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.600 --> 01:41.800
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:41.940 --> 01:47.140
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:41.940 --> 01:47.140
The crimson kiss

01:47.250 --> 01:54.080
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.250 --> 01:54.080
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.250 --> 02:00.050
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.250 --> 02:00.050
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:08.900 --> 02:11.260
That man in the picture.

02:11.370 --> 02:14.800
He was a patient at my grandfather's hospital.

02:14.900 --> 02:16.840
My grandfather, without hesitation

02:16.940 --> 02:20.740
let the penniless patient stay for eight years.

02:20.840 --> 02:22.500
Do you know why?

02:23.350 --> 02:27.410
Without eating or drinking,
and with no sleep at all

02:27.520 --> 02:29.310
he had lived for eight years.

02:29.420 --> 02:30.750
What?!

02:30.850 --> 02:34.250
I've searched many years
and have finally met him.

02:34.360 --> 02:37.520
He looks exactly as he does in the picture.

02:37.630 --> 02:41.320
Still the beautiful figure that he
was when he committed suicide

02:41.430 --> 02:44.030
on that snowy night 72 years ago.

02:44.120 --> 02:49.160
Episode 11: The Kyoto Arc, Part 2

03:26.940 --> 03:28.840
Tsuzuki.

03:32.120 --> 03:34.350
Tsuzu... ki...

03:37.750 --> 03:41.210
Hey, Tsuzuki! Tsuzuki!

03:46.360 --> 03:47.690
A dream...?

03:57.310 --> 03:58.400
Tsuzuki...

03:58.530 --> 04:06.490
Signs: Fortune telling, charms, etc.

04:10.390 --> 04:12.050
<i>Oh, Tsuzuki-san...</i>

04:12.160 --> 04:14.950
<i>I see you wear your watch on your right wrist.</i>

04:15.060 --> 04:16.790
<i>Is that because you're a lefty?</i>

04:16.890 --> 04:19.690
<i>Or is it to hide the scars on your wrist?</i>

04:20.160 --> 04:22.890
<i>Yeah. That's right, Muraki.</i>

04:23.330 --> 04:28.130
<i>I wanted to die.
I slit my wrists over and over.</i>

04:29.770 --> 04:32.830
<i>But I wasn't able to die.</i>

04:32.940 --> 04:36.610
How unlike you to be walking
the Philosopher's Path.

04:38.350 --> 04:40.840
How about a little fortune-telling?

04:40.950 --> 04:42.280
Hisoka...

04:42.790 --> 04:43.910
Have this.

04:44.020 --> 04:46.720
You come up with bad ideas
on an empty stomach.

04:46.820 --> 04:48.350
Especially in your case.

04:48.460 --> 04:49.790
Maybe...

04:50.660 --> 04:51.630
Delicious!

04:51.730 --> 04:54.820
Delicious, huh? That's good.

04:55.360 --> 04:59.300
Thanks, Hisoka.
I'll be all right now.

05:00.600 --> 05:02.470
You're not being fair.

05:03.910 --> 05:08.500
When it comes to strangers,
you won't hesitate and charge right in.

05:08.610 --> 05:11.770
But you hide everything
about yourself. That's cowardly.

05:11.880 --> 05:13.510
I suppose.

05:13.920 --> 05:17.510
If it means inviting the
scorn of you and the others

05:17.620 --> 05:22.080
having you all know the truth
about me, I prefer this.

05:22.190 --> 05:25.820
I don't care if I'm a cowardly
man who cheats himself.

05:26.200 --> 05:28.220
<i>Can't he trust me?</i>

05:28.330 --> 05:32.670
<i>Does he think I'm not worthy
of talking it over with?</i>

05:34.000 --> 05:35.630
<i>You fool.</i>

05:38.010 --> 05:40.570
Hey, Tsuzuki! Hey, kid!

05:40.680 --> 05:41.700
Watari?

05:41.810 --> 05:43.750
It's time for work.

05:43.850 --> 05:46.140
I've got some information about Muraki.

05:59.700 --> 06:01.420
Morning practice?

06:01.700 --> 06:03.290
You could say that.

06:03.520 --> 06:05.330
What are you doing?

06:05.430 --> 06:08.270
I'm moving onto my final preparations.

06:09.140 --> 06:10.110
I see.

06:10.440 --> 06:14.070
No one can stop me now.

06:16.180 --> 06:19.010
No one can stop him, huh?

06:20.080 --> 06:22.640
Muraki's practice is in Tokyo

06:22.750 --> 06:25.850
but he comes to the university
in Kyoto once a month.

06:26.060 --> 06:30.790
He comes to see his mentor
from his student days, Dr. Satomi.

06:30.890 --> 06:33.020
Pretty good detective work.

06:33.130 --> 06:38.230
You see the grocer about produce,
a doctor about doctors.

06:38.330 --> 06:40.670
Well, there it is.

06:40.770 --> 06:42.260
Shion University

06:42.370 --> 06:45.860
where they do the most
advanced clone research in Japan.

06:45.980 --> 06:47.530
Clone research?

06:47.640 --> 06:49.700
It seems way too suspicious.

06:55.790 --> 06:57.840
Oops, another dead end.

06:57.950 --> 07:00.720
Hey, when are we
going to get there?

07:00.820 --> 07:02.090
Can we help you?

07:02.190 --> 07:04.920
Uh, where is the university?

07:05.030 --> 07:08.520
The university?
This is the affiliated high school.

07:08.630 --> 07:09.830
Affiliated high school?

07:09.930 --> 07:12.770
Watari, you've got no
sense of direction, do you?

07:12.870 --> 07:14.930
The university's in the opposite direction.

07:15.040 --> 07:16.940
If you'd like, we can take you there.

07:19.580 --> 07:22.010
This is Dr. Satomi's laboratory.

07:22.110 --> 07:23.870
Thanks.
You really helped us.

07:23.980 --> 07:25.450
It's nothing.

07:25.550 --> 07:30.580
<i>Without eating or drinking,
and with no sleep at all</i>

07:30.690 --> 07:33.180
<i>he had lived for eight years.</i>

07:33.290 --> 07:35.220
<i>How about it, Doctor?</i>

07:35.320 --> 07:38.090
<i>Don't you think he'd make
a wonderful specimen?</i>

07:38.190 --> 07:41.460
How could a dream like this be real?

07:41.660 --> 07:42.860
Come on.

07:43.930 --> 07:45.960
Are you Dr. Satomi?

07:46.440 --> 07:49.170
We have a few questions
about Muraki Kazutaka,

07:49.270 --> 07:51.500
a former student of yours.

07:52.110 --> 07:54.910
I understand he visits you every month.

07:55.010 --> 07:59.410
You must be mistaken.
He's never come around here.

07:59.520 --> 08:02.420
I believe you've been doing clone research?

08:02.520 --> 08:06.820
Uh, yes. Although I prefer
not to divulge any details.

08:06.920 --> 08:09.580
- Can't blame you.
- Is that all?

08:09.690 --> 08:12.560
I have something after this.

08:12.660 --> 08:13.630
Uh, wait a sec...

08:14.860 --> 08:16.490
What the...?

08:19.240 --> 08:23.100
He's alive.
He really is alive.

08:26.810 --> 08:29.970
Muraki-kun! He really is alive!

08:30.080 --> 08:31.710
Did he come?

08:31.810 --> 08:33.780
Yes. But don't worry.

08:33.880 --> 08:36.820
I didn't tell him anything about you.

08:36.920 --> 08:41.620
More importantly, I want him!
I want him as my specimen!

08:41.820 --> 08:43.050
I understand.

08:43.160 --> 08:44.180
Now...

08:44.290 --> 08:48.420
I'll be able to show those
bastards who laughed at me.

08:56.110 --> 08:57.900
That doctor stinks.

08:58.270 --> 09:03.010
Yeah. I felt fear and denial in him.

09:03.580 --> 09:08.950
Anyway, we'll keep an eye on him
and wait for Muraki to make his move.

09:09.050 --> 09:11.210
- Hey.
- What?

09:11.320 --> 09:14.920
Shall I tell you the result of
this morning's fortune-telling?

09:15.020 --> 09:17.490
Sure. Tell me! Tell me!

09:17.690 --> 09:20.160
Compatibility between you and I.

09:20.930 --> 09:23.420
The biggest and worst...

09:24.630 --> 09:25.930
black omen.

09:28.640 --> 09:30.130
Terrible...

09:30.240 --> 09:34.110
But I don't think it'll get worse than this.

09:34.210 --> 09:36.440
We've gone as far as we can.

09:36.910 --> 09:39.780
We just have to climb now.

09:49.230 --> 09:53.320
The Fushimi Inarini Shrine is a
shrine for the god of merchants.

09:53.430 --> 09:57.530
Well, we wouldn't really want
our business to pick up though.

09:57.630 --> 10:00.730
You didn't have to buy
all of that at once.

10:00.840 --> 10:02.930
I know, but...

10:03.040 --> 10:05.130
Hey, there's a shooting range!

10:05.610 --> 10:07.630
Good grief. He's like a kid.

10:09.810 --> 10:11.180
Good evening.

10:11.280 --> 10:12.540
Thanks for earlier.

10:13.020 --> 10:15.920
I'll get you a present as gratitude.

10:16.590 --> 10:17.550
Really?

10:21.720 --> 10:23.560
Come on!
Hit the darn thing!

10:27.800 --> 10:28.890
Wow! You're so good!

10:36.940 --> 10:39.770
- I know.
- How lucky!

10:42.950 --> 10:46.850
Excuse me, young ladies...

10:46.950 --> 10:50.680
Did you happen to see
a man dressed in black?

10:50.790 --> 10:52.380
That man...

10:52.490 --> 10:53.920
Dressed in black?

10:54.020 --> 10:57.120
Oh, the people who were
looking for Dr. Satomi.

10:57.230 --> 10:59.590
I see.

11:00.260 --> 11:04.390
How unfortunate that you saw...

11:05.030 --> 11:06.560
that Shinigami.

11:12.470 --> 11:15.740
The more you get upset
about this, the more you'll miss.

11:15.850 --> 11:18.810
Shut up! I'll get it if I have to kill myself!

11:35.000 --> 11:39.130
Tsuzuki-san, I've come to get you.

11:39.900 --> 11:44.450
Yami no Matsuei

11:48.210 --> 11:51.040
Maki... Maki...!

11:52.250 --> 11:55.050
Tsuzuki-san, isn't it wonderful?

11:55.650 --> 12:00.350
These vultures just love human flesh.

12:00.960 --> 12:02.510
Poor thing.

12:02.930 --> 12:06.330
She died because she saw a Shinigami.

12:08.930 --> 12:12.920
What's the matter, Tsuzuki-san?
Is this too painful?

12:15.240 --> 12:18.400
Let's get going, Tsuzuki-san.

12:18.970 --> 12:20.870
Tsuzuki! Get out of here!

12:22.380 --> 12:24.210
Again because of me...

12:25.350 --> 12:26.440
Tsuzuki!

12:32.820 --> 12:34.250
What?!

12:37.290 --> 12:40.630
I'm sorry to disturb your fun.

12:40.730 --> 12:41.700
Tatsumi-san...

12:41.800 --> 12:43.860
But I won't allow you

12:43.970 --> 12:48.270
to put this man in any further danger, Doctor.

12:48.370 --> 12:49.670
Tatsumi...

12:49.770 --> 12:53.540
Don't worry.
I'll take care of that doctor.

12:53.740 --> 12:55.870
I'm really sorry.

12:57.310 --> 13:01.810
So, you are the secretary
of the great Ministry of Hades?

13:01.920 --> 13:06.650
I'm so glad we have an
opportunity to meet, Tatsumi-san.

13:06.760 --> 13:08.720
The same goes for me.

13:08.820 --> 13:13.450
Quite the pleasure to meet a doctor
with such an evil reputation.

13:14.230 --> 13:17.600
An unsparing man you are.
As I thought.

13:17.770 --> 13:21.100
And it's not just my mouth that's unsparing.

13:27.710 --> 13:33.080
I'm the type who prefers to
completely wipe out those I don't like.

13:33.180 --> 13:36.170
And you went after
one of our employees.

13:36.290 --> 13:38.620
I could never allow that!

13:39.490 --> 13:42.220
You seem quite passionate about it.

13:42.320 --> 13:43.310
Silence!

13:43.890 --> 13:49.850
That's expected of a Shinigami.
So hard to catch.

13:49.970 --> 13:53.030
My clothes have gotten dirty.

13:53.400 --> 13:56.370
You'll have to excuse me today.

14:10.250 --> 14:12.580
Have you woken up, Tsuzuki-san?

14:12.690 --> 14:16.990
- Tatsumi... Where am I?
- A hotel room.

14:17.560 --> 14:19.990
Don't worry about the bill.

14:20.100 --> 14:22.430
I'll pay with my credit card.

14:23.630 --> 14:25.290
What about that girl?

14:25.400 --> 14:28.030
I took her back to her home.

14:28.200 --> 14:29.760
I see.

14:33.140 --> 14:34.200
Tsuzuki-san!

14:34.310 --> 14:36.370
Another person died.

14:36.480 --> 14:40.880
Because of me... Muraki killed her
because she talked to me.

14:40.980 --> 14:45.750
Don't blame yourself for this.
You've done nothing wrong.

14:46.220 --> 14:47.950
But still...

14:48.190 --> 14:51.520
It's not like you to cry like this. Be a man.

14:51.990 --> 14:55.020
I'm sorry... But still...

14:55.200 --> 14:59.930
Don't you worry about a thing.
Now, just get some rest.

15:00.040 --> 15:01.000
Tatsumi...

15:01.100 --> 15:04.300
What you need now is rest.

15:04.410 --> 15:05.530
Thank you.

15:09.810 --> 15:13.370
I'll make you pay physically
for hurting Tsuzuki.

15:14.050 --> 15:15.350
Muraki Kazutaka!

15:24.490 --> 15:26.690
<i>He was terrified.</i>

15:26.800 --> 15:28.850
<i>His spirit was quivering.</i>

15:29.360 --> 15:31.330
<i>He was deeply wounded.</i>

15:32.570 --> 15:33.930
<i>What should I do?</i>

15:34.040 --> 15:39.340
<i>I've never consoled anybody, nor
tried to cheer anybody up ever.</i>

15:40.040 --> 15:41.770
How's Tsuzuki?

15:41.880 --> 15:44.870
He seems quite upset right now.

15:44.980 --> 15:47.280
He'll be all right once he rests.

15:47.380 --> 15:48.370
I see.

15:48.650 --> 15:52.810
You must be exhausted as well.
You should go to bed.

15:53.060 --> 15:54.390
Tatsumi-san.

15:54.490 --> 15:58.690
I'm going to go with Watari-san to see Dr. Satomi.

16:00.000 --> 16:04.830
So, Tatsumi-san, will you stay close to him?

16:04.930 --> 16:08.270
I've never seen Tsuzuki like that

16:08.370 --> 16:13.100
and, well, I just don't know
how to deal with him.

16:13.210 --> 16:17.870
I might end up saying
something that will hurt him.

16:18.150 --> 16:22.880
You've known him much longer,
so he'll feel better with you around.

16:23.220 --> 16:28.450
I only lasted three months
when I teamed up with him.

16:28.560 --> 16:31.860
I think you have a much
better understanding of him.

16:32.290 --> 16:33.260
But still...

16:33.360 --> 16:38.100
Kurosaki. What's important
is not the length of time.

16:38.470 --> 16:41.230
And, at the very least...

16:41.340 --> 16:45.800
you learned something about
compassion after meeting Tsuzuki-san.

16:47.310 --> 16:51.270
You just have to do for
Tsuzuki-san what he did for you.

16:51.380 --> 16:52.350
Tatsumi-san...

16:52.450 --> 16:56.940
However, I will accept your request.

16:57.050 --> 16:59.540
But next time, you do it yourself.

16:59.660 --> 17:03.090
He'd appreciate that much more.

17:12.130 --> 17:14.730
Don't we stand out like sore thumbs?

17:14.840 --> 17:19.770
There's nothing to worry about.
We are customers after all.

17:19.980 --> 17:23.570
When I was told to come to
Kyoto in place of Gushoushin,

17:23.680 --> 17:26.270
I was asked from all over to bring back gifts.

17:27.150 --> 17:29.010
Tatsumi, isn't this enough?

17:29.120 --> 17:32.550
Hisoka's going to be pissed at
me unless I get back to work.

17:32.650 --> 17:35.850
Not to worry.
Kurosaki-kun has official status.

17:36.490 --> 17:37.580
Hisoka does?

17:37.690 --> 17:41.930
Yes. You will be spending the day with me.

17:42.030 --> 17:45.590
We'll hear from him,
so there's nothing to worry about.

18:02.720 --> 18:06.120
There's no doubt Muraki's involved with Satomi.

18:06.320 --> 18:08.980
How do we get Satomi to fess up to that?

18:09.090 --> 18:12.080
Leave it to me.
I've got a great idea.

18:17.200 --> 18:19.330
Was Muraki-kun here?

18:19.900 --> 18:21.030
Muraki-kun?

18:21.570 --> 18:22.540
You people?!

18:22.640 --> 18:25.630
That's not the same story you told us before.

18:25.740 --> 18:27.940
You said you didn't know Muraki.

18:28.040 --> 18:30.240
Shut up! I'll call the police!

18:30.350 --> 18:34.510
Fine. But I think you'll be
the one to get into trouble.

18:34.820 --> 18:38.150
Do you know how Muraki got hold of this?

18:38.350 --> 18:40.150
Wh-What are you talking about?

18:40.260 --> 18:43.880
Take a look at a newspaper
if you want to know. Bye.

18:47.000 --> 18:48.860
Who are those guys...?

18:55.240 --> 18:57.170
Tired, Tsuzuki-san?

18:57.270 --> 19:01.900
Not at all. I haven't had
this much fun in quite a while.

19:02.380 --> 19:04.310
Well, that's good.

19:06.320 --> 19:07.510
Hey.

19:07.620 --> 19:11.810
We came here for tea a lot
when we were working together.

19:11.920 --> 19:15.120
This town has sure changed since back then.

19:15.220 --> 19:16.280
Yes.

19:16.390 --> 19:19.090
Tatsumi. Thanks for today.

19:19.190 --> 19:21.690
That sad look doesn't suit you.

19:21.960 --> 19:25.730
I suppose. It's not going to do
any good for me to sulk like this.

19:25.830 --> 19:28.060
I'll just end up falling into his trap.

19:29.170 --> 19:30.870
Tatsumi...

19:30.970 --> 19:35.970
I don't want to create more
sad memories of this city.

19:36.080 --> 19:40.810
As long as Muraki's alive,
he will go after that girl.

19:40.920 --> 19:45.350
He's not going to kill her.
I'll be sure to protect that girl!

19:53.300 --> 19:56.530
That Mariko was apparently
with Maki when she was killed.

19:56.630 --> 19:59.570
I heard the police were investigating her.

19:59.670 --> 20:01.860
Maybe Mariko killed Maki.

20:02.000 --> 20:04.230
No. It wasn't me!

20:04.340 --> 20:08.070
I saw it.
I saw that man kill Maki.

20:08.510 --> 20:11.240
Now, boys and girls

20:11.350 --> 20:15.580
let me introduce the temporary
teachers who have joined us

20:15.680 --> 20:18.740
as well as some of the transfer students.

20:19.920 --> 20:22.620
I am the eldest brother.
Tatsumi Seiichiro.

20:22.720 --> 20:24.660
I'll be teaching math.

20:24.760 --> 20:28.130
I'm Asato, number two.
I'll be teaching social studies.

20:28.230 --> 20:30.200
I'm number three. Yutaka.

20:30.300 --> 20:32.100
I'll be teaching science.
Nice to meet you.

20:32.200 --> 20:33.830
I'm the youngest. Hisoka.

20:35.400 --> 20:38.400
<i>Why are these guys in this school?!</i>

20:41.710 --> 20:46.040
<i>Are they after me?
At this rate, I'll be killed.</i>

20:46.150 --> 20:48.410
<i>I'll be killed by the Shinigami.</i>

20:54.490 --> 20:56.580
<i>Take a look at a newspaper
if you want to know.</i>

20:56.690 --> 21:00.290
Mutilated body of woman
found in the Kamo River.

21:00.400 --> 21:04.460
The fact that a lock of hair
was cut from the victim

21:04.570 --> 21:07.870
suggests this was the work
of a serial murderer,

21:07.970 --> 21:11.370
who has been committing
these crimes in the Kyoto area.

21:11.840 --> 21:15.440
A lock of hair was cut from the victim?!

21:20.680 --> 21:22.170
Tsuzuki-san...

21:23.080 --> 21:26.880
You'll go that far to protect others?

21:27.420 --> 21:29.950
You are so truly kind.

21:30.890 --> 21:34.260
That kindness will be your downfall.

21:36.230 --> 21:38.930
Well, isn't that right, Saki?

21:40.420 --> 21:43.460
Next Episode

21:42.540 --> 21:44.630
A past that can't be touched.

21:44.740 --> 21:46.000
I cannot see anything.

21:46.310 --> 21:48.070
I could not protect myself.

21:48.180 --> 21:50.440
I cannot hear anything.

21:50.550 --> 21:53.280
Tsuzuki, who had fallen
into the trap set by Muraki...

21:53.380 --> 21:57.340
The darkness comes again.

22:01.420 --> 22:10.370
Episode 12   The Kyoto Arc, Part 3

22:01.420 --> 22:05.380
Next time on Yami no Matsuei: The Kyoto Arc, Part 3.

22:05.960 --> 22:09.190
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.710 --> 22:22.070
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.710 --> 22:22.070
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:22.180 --> 22:25.110
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:22.180 --> 22:25.110
I wait for you on the street corner

22:25.210 --> 22:28.700
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:25.210 --> 22:28.700
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.820 --> 22:31.410
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.820 --> 22:31.410
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.520 --> 22:38.750
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.520 --> 22:38.750
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.860 --> 22:45.490
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.860 --> 22:45.490
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.950 --> 23:05.370
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.950 --> 23:05.370
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

23:05.890 --> 23:11.820
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

23:05.890 --> 23:11.820
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

23:12.590 --> 23:18.930
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

23:12.590 --> 23:18.930
No one could possibly recognize the melody

23:19.680 --> 23:25.080
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

23:19.680 --> 23:25.080
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
